OL,3,ADeadly shark attack prompts rare kill
OL,4,Aorder in Western Australia
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rare catch-and-kill order has been
OL,7,Fissued for a great white shark off the
OL,8,Fcoast of Western Australia, after a man
OL,9,Fwas killed while on a morning swim at a
OL,10,Fpopular beach on Friday. His body has
OL,11,Fstill not been found.
OL,13,FAuthorities have said that beaches
OL,14,Falong the state's coast, including in
OL,15,Fthe capital Perth, will remain closed
OL,16,Funtil at least Sunday as the search for
OL,17,Fthe shark continues.
OL,19,FIt is the second shark attack in
OL,20,FWestern Australia (WA) this week, and
OL,21,Fthe third fatal attack in the state
OL,22,Fthis year.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
